# Git-secrets allowed patterns for legitimate code and documentation
# These patterns are safe and should not be blocked

# Environment variable references in code (safe - not hardcoded)
Bearer \$\{process\.env\.[A-Z_]+\}

# Authentication header checks in code (safe - checking format)
\.startsWith\('Bearer '\)

# Documentation examples (safe - not real secrets)
Bearer eyJ\[a-zA-Z0-9_-\]
eyJ\*

# Pre-commit hook patterns (safe - documentation)
Bearer eyJ\[a-zA-Z0-9\]

# CLAUDE.md documentation patterns (safe - examples in security documentation)
"❌ BLOCKED: Hardcoded Bearer token detected"

# Server routes authentication patterns (safe - documentation comment)
For now, allow access with any Bearer token

# Vertex AI OAuth token patterns (safe - dynamically generated by Google Auth library)
Bearer \$\{accessToken
Authorization.*Bearer.*\$\{accessToken

# Tools authentication patterns (safe - hardcoded placeholder tokens for staff endpoints)
Bearer staff-token
Authorization.*Bearer.*staff-token